### Phase 1 walking-skeleton smoke test.
### Works with VS Code's "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ's built-in HTTP client:
### run requests top to bottom - each one captures a variable the next one needs.
### Assumes `docker compose up` is running (or each service via `./gradlew bootRun` locally).

@tenantBaseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@orderBaseUrl = http://localhost:8082


### 1. Onboard a tenant. No auth required - this is how an identity is created
### in the first place.
# @name onboard
POST {{tenantBaseUrl}}/tenants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Distributors"
}

###

@tenantId = {{onboard.response.body.id}}


### 2. Log in as that tenant. Phase 1 simplification: no password yet, just
### prove you know an onboarded tenant id (see LoginRequest's Javadoc).
# @name login
POST {{tenantBaseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}"
}

###

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}


### 3. Confirm the token works against Tenant Service itself.
GET {{tenantBaseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###


### 4. Fetch the (hardcoded, Phase 1) catalog.
GET {{tenantBaseUrl}}/catalog/{{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###


### 5. Happy path: place an order. This is the saga's main event - watch
### `docker compose logs -f order-inventory-service credit-service invoice-service`
### while running this to see the same X-Correlation-Id thread through all
### three services, and the order progress PLACED -> CREDIT_LOCKED ->
### STOCK_RESERVED -> COMPLETED.
### Expect: 201, status COMPLETED, a non-null invoiceId.
POST {{orderBaseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-001", "qty": 2, "unitPrice": 4500.00 }
  ]
}

###


### 6. Forced failure + compensation: simulateStockFailure=true always fails
### the (stubbed) stock check after credit has already been locked, forcing
### the saga's one Phase 1 compensating action: releasing that credit lock.
### Expect: 422, status STOCK_REJECTED, invoiceId null.
### Verify the compensation actually ran with:
###   docker exec <postgres-container> psql -U postgres -d credit_db \
###     -c "SELECT order_id, status FROM credit_locks ORDER BY created_at;"
### - the lock for THIS order should show RELEASED, not LOCKED.
POST {{orderBaseUrl}}/orders?simulateStockFailure=true
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-002", "qty": 5, "unitPrice": 380.00 }
  ]
}

###


### 7. Same request without a token - every endpoint except onboarding and
### login requires one. Expect: 403.
POST {{orderBaseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-001", "qty": 1, "unitPrice": 4500.00 }
  ]
}

###
